\section{Dominance Frontiers}\label{sec:dominance-frontiers-ssa}

Dominance frontiers are the key concept linking dominance to SSA construction.

\subsection{Intuition}\label{sec:df-intuition}

The dominance frontier of a block $D$ is the set of blocks where $D$'s dominance ``ends.'' If a variable is defined in $D$, its value may be ``overwritten'' at blocks in $\mathrm{DF}(D)$ by a different definition reaching from another path.

\subsection{Computing Dominance Frontiers}\label{sec:df-computation}

\begin{algorithm}[H]
\caption{Dominance Frontier Computation}\label{alg:df-computation}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\Function{ComputeDF}{$\mathrm{CFG}$}
  \For{each block $B$ with $\geq 2$ predecessors}
    \For{each predecessor $P$ of $B$}
      \State $\mathrm{runner} \gets P$
      \While{$\mathrm{runner} \neq \mathrm{idom}(B)$}
        \State $\mathrm{DF}(\mathrm{runner}) \gets \mathrm{DF}(\mathrm{runner}) \cup \{B\}$
        \State $\mathrm{runner} \gets \mathrm{idom}(\mathrm{runner})$
      \EndWhile
    \EndFor
  \EndFor
  \State \Return $\mathrm{DF}$
\EndFunction
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

