\begin{insight}
The key insight of SSA form is that making data dependencies explicit transforms global analyses into local pattern matching. In non-SSA form, determining which definition reaches a use requires a global dataflow analysis. In SSA form, the reaching definition is simply the variable being used---it is right there in the instruction. This locality is what makes SSA-based optimizations so effective and so easy to implement. Memory SSA extends this insight to the memory domain, treating the entire memory state as a single variable that flows through the program.
\end{insight}

