\section{Summary and Further Reading}\label{sec:summary-56}

SSA form is the cornerstone of modern compiler optimization. By ensuring that every variable is assigned exactly once, it makes data dependencies explicit and enables local optimization techniques. The construction algorithm, based on dominance frontiers, is efficient and well-understood. The out-of-SSA translation, with coalescing, produces efficient machine code.

For further reading, we recommend the original Cytron et al. paper~\cite{cytron1991}, the comprehensive survey by Braun~\cite{braun2013}, and the LLVM documentation on SSA.
